# openOODA x86 Per-Shape Coverage Matrix — depth pass on the v2 hostile-probe top 5

Logline: For each of the 5 most-miscompiled source shapes from x86-hostile-probe-v2.oot, count fixtures, classify compile outcome, expose the sub-distribution, and rank fixes by silent-miscompile impact.

Setup: Re-reads the v2 outcome table (`/tmp/x86probe2/x86.txt`, 6,936 rows) and run output (`/tmp/x86probe2/run.txt`, 5,750 rows) and exit code (`/tmp/x86probe2/run_rc.txt`). Crosses these against per-fixture source under `ooda/fixtures/*.oo`. Detection is regex-based on the .oo source; the v2 detectors are not on disk, so totals here diverge from v2 §5 by ±5% on Float, ±10% on 3-arm match and struct (see Caveats).

Beats:
  1. Top 5 shape table — fixture count, pass, no-op, ASM-FAIL, refused, success rate.
  2. Per-shape sub-distribution — 2-5 sub-shapes per top shape, with success rate.
  3. Simple vs complex — 1 row per shape, splits each shape into single-use vs multi-use.
  4. Recommended per-shape fix — one concrete fix per top shape, ordered by impact.
  5. Top 3 highest-impact sub-shapes — ranked by silent-miscompile count.
  6. Caveats — detector mismatches vs v2 and known biases.

File: openOODA/audit/x86-shape-coverage.oot
THIS FILE IS GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT. Source: x86 hostile probe v2 2026-08-25 plus per-shape scan.

