# # 1. Top 5 shapes — coverage table

Per-fixture classification:
  - pass       = COMPILED in `x86.txt` AND non-`(empty)` first-line in `run.txt`.
  - no-op      = COMPILED in `x86.txt` AND `(empty)` first-line in `run.txt` AND rc=0.
  - asm-fail   = ASM-FAIL in `x86.txt`.
  - refused    = REFUSED in `x86.txt`.

The "(empty) → no-op main" finding from v2 §4 dominates the silent-miscompile column.

| # | Shape | Fixtures | pass | no-op (silent) | ASM-FAIL | REFUSED | Success rate |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Float (any) | 592 | 2 | 156 | 0 | 434 | 0.3% |
| 2 | 3-arm match | 16 | 6 | 6 | 0 | 4 | 37.5% |
| 3 | Result[T] | 241 | 37 | 179 | 0 | 25 | 15.4% |
| 4 | struct | 75 | 4 | 47 | 0 | 24 | 5.3% |
| 5 | List[T] | 264 | 40 | 162 | 0 | 62 | 15.2% |
| — | total-with-any-top-shape | 1,188 | 89 | 550 | 0 | 549 | 7.5% |

Cross-check vs v2 §5 (denominator / silent-miscompile):
  - Float  158/160  — my count 156/592; my detector catches any `Float` token, v2 catches const-fold only.
  - 3-arm  27/30   — my count 6/16; v2 has a different match-arm detector (see Caveats).
  - Result 179/216  — my count 179/241; close.
  - struct 224/277  — my count 47/75; v2's "field/type" includes field-access + type-name, which I split (see §2).
  - List   162/202  — my count 162/264; close.

The 592-vs-160 gap on Float, and 75-vs-277 on struct, is detector breadth (see Caveats), not fixture disagreement. The "no-op" column is the count of fixtures that COMPILED then ran with empty stdout — these are the silent miscompiles the orchestrator must convert to visible REFUSED or fix to pass.

